  "summary": "Against the king-pawn opening, Black gives a pawn for rapid development and wins it back with active pieces.",
  "goal": {
    "title": "Win the pawn back by developing fast",
    "text": "Black is a pawn down on purpose. The plan is to bring pieces out with threats: the bishop jumps to the side of the board and hits White's queen, a knight attacks the extra pawn, and soon Black regains it with more active pieces. Do not waste time retreating; every move should develop a piece or hit something.",
    "plans": [
      "Win back the extra pawn quickly with a knight or the queen.",
      "Keep the bishop outside the pawn chain, where it stays active.",
      "Bring out the rest of the pieces at once: a pawn move to free the bishop, the knight, then castle.",
      "Do not spend moves chasing with the queen."
    ],
